[Debug] ----- Vuln Cause Analysis -----
The potential vulnerability is related to a Denial of Service (DoS) vulnerability. This vulnerability arises from the handling of file uploads, specifically when processing zip files. If the application does not impose strict limits on the size or number of files within the zip, an attacker could upload a maliciously crafted zip file containing excessively large files or a large number of files, which could exhaust server resources such as memory and CPU. This could lead to the application becoming unresponsive or crashing, thereby denying service to legitimate users. The lack of proper validation and resource management when dealing with file uploads is the underlying cause of this vulnerability.

